We have
\begin{align*} \frac{\sec x}{\sin x} - \frac{\sin x}{\cos x} &= \frac{1}{\cos x} \cdot \frac{1}{\sin x} - \frac{\sin x}{\cos x} \\ &= \frac{1}{\sin x \cos x} - \frac{\sin x}{\cos x} \\ &= \frac{1 - \sin^2 x}{\sin x \cos x} \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin x \cos x} \\ &= \frac{\cos x}{\sin x} \\ &= \cot x. \end{align*}
Therefore,
\[ \frac{\sec x}{\sin x} - \frac{\sin x}{\cos x} = \cot x. \]

\boxed{\cot x}
